The original is already a bounds check plus an address computation, so the gain here is small. This version uses `data() + i` in place of `&fields[index]`, which skips the `operator[]` call path in unoptimized builds and gives the same result for every input.

```cpp
const Field* Mesg::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index) const
{
    const std::size_t i = static_cast<std::size_t>(index);
    if (i < fields.size())
        return fields.data() + i;

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```